---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Hindi Muhavare aur Lokoktiyan - LogicPath Systems">
    <section class="legal-page" style="padding-top: 120px; min-height: 100vh;">
        <div class="container reveal">
            <div class="glass-card" style="padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);">
                <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
                    <h1 class="gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Hindi Muhavare aur Lokoktiyan</strong></p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Effective date:</strong> 12 October 2026</p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>App:</strong> Hindi Muhavare aur Lokoktiyan (Android package com.logicpathsystems.hindimuhavare)</p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Developer:</strong> LogicPath Systems · <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">contact@logicpathsystems.com</a></p>
                </header>

                <main class="legal-content">
                    <p>This policy explains what information the app uses, why, and the choices you have.</p>

                    <h2>1. Summary</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>No account, sign-in, location, contacts, camera, microphone or file access.</li>
                        <li>Your learning data (bookmarks, quiz history, settings) stays on your device.</li>
                        <li>The app is free and shows ads through Google AdMob.</li>
                        <li>The app uses Google Firebase Analytics to understand, in aggregate, how the app is used. You can turn this off in Settings.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>2. Information stored only on your device</h2>
                    <p>The app stores the following in its private storage on your phone. It is not sent to us or to anyone else:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>bookmarked idioms and proverbs, and up to 50 recently read entries;</li>
                        <li>quiz progress, up to 100 completed quiz results (date and score) and the list of wrongly answered questions;</li>
                        <li>settings (theme, text size, analytics on/off) and whether the app has been opened before.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Android cloud backup is disabled for this data. You can delete it from Settings → clear history, from Android Settings → Apps → Clear data, or by uninstalling the app.</p>

                    <h2>3. Advertising — Google AdMob</h2>
                    <p>The app shows <strong>banner ads</strong>, <strong>app open ads</strong> (a full-screen ad shown when the app is opened or brought back to the screen; it is not shown on the first launch after install and can be closed) and <strong>interstitial ads</strong> (a full-screen ad that can be closed, shown occasionally when a practice quiz ends, before its result; not after your first quiz). Ads are provided by Google AdMob.</p>
                    <p>To show and measure ads and to prevent fraud, the Google Mobile Ads SDK may collect and process:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>the device's advertising ID (Android Advertising ID);</li>
                        <li>IP address and approximate location derived from it;</li>
                        <li>device and app information (device model, OS version, language, app version);</li>
                        <li>ad interaction data (ad impressions and clicks), diagnostics and crash data related to ads.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Consent:</strong> if you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, or another region where the law requires it, the app shows Google's consent form before any ads are requested. You can change your choice at any time from <strong>Settings → Ad privacy choices</strong> (shown where applicable). If you do not consent to personalised ads, Google may still show non-personalised ads, which use contextual information only.</p>
                    <p>You can also reset or delete your advertising ID, or opt out of ad personalisation, in <strong>Android Settings → Google → Ads</strong> (or Settings → Privacy → Ads).</p>
                    <p>How Google uses data: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a><br/>Google Privacy Policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a></p>

                    <h2>4. Analytics — Google Firebase Analytics</h2>
                    <p>The app uses Firebase Analytics to see, in aggregate, which screens are used and how practice quizzes are used, so we can improve the content. Firebase may collect:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>an app-instance identifier (generated by Firebase) and, where permitted, the advertising ID;</li>
                        <li>screen views (for example "library", "practice", "entry") and app events such as first open, session start, quiz started and quiz completed (with the number of questions and score);</li>
                        <li>device model, OS version, language, app version, approximate country/region from the IP address, and session length.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>We do not send your bookmarks, the text you search for, your name or any contact details to Firebase. Analytics data is used only in aggregate and is not used to identify you. Firebase retains it for the period set in our Firebase project (at most 14 months).</p>
                    <p><strong>Opt out:</strong> turn off <strong>Settings → Share usage statistics</strong> in the app. Collection stops on that device until you turn it on again.</p>
                    <p>Firebase privacy information: <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy</a></p>

                    <h2>5. Sharing of information</h2>
                    <p>We do not sell personal information. Information described in sections 3 and 4 is processed by Google LLC as our advertising and analytics provider, under Google's terms. We do not otherwise share information, except where required by law.</p>

                    <h2>6. Data security</h2>
                    <p>Data sent to Google is encrypted in transit (HTTPS). Data on your device is held in the app's private storage, which other apps cannot read.</p>

                    <h2>7. Children</h2>
                    <p>The app is a general educational reference intended for students aged 13 and above and for adults. It is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has used the app in a way that resulted in data collection, contact us and we will help remove it.</p>

                    <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
                    <p>Depending on where you live (for example under the EU/UK GDPR or India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023), you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal data and to withdraw consent. Because we do not hold an account or personal profile for you, most data can be controlled directly through the options above (clearing app data, the analytics switch, ad privacy choices and Android ad settings). For requests about data processed by Google, contact us or use Google's tools at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://myaccount.google.com</a>.</p>

                    <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
                    <p>We may update this policy when the app changes. The new version will be published at the same address with a new effective date and will be available inside the app.</p>

                    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
                    <p>LogicPath Systems — <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">contact@logicpathsystems.com</a></p>

                    <p style="margin-top: 2.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;">Effective 12 October 2026. © LogicPath Systems.</p>
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal-content h2, .legal-content h3 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .legal-content h2 {
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content h3 {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .legal-content p, .legal-content ul {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-content ul {
        padding-left: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .legal-content li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content a {
        color: var(--primary);
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    .legal-content a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }
</style>
